# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Next.js side (.env.local) — generated by `npx convex dev`; no manual edits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=

# If a stale `.env.production.local` also defines NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL, the
# Convex CLI warns that it "cannot update automatically" and a local
# `next build` silently points at production. Delete that file — on Vercel the
# URL is injected by `npx convex deploy --cmd 'npm run build'` (see vercel.json).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Convex deployment side — set with `npx convex env set NAME value`
#    (add --prod for the production deployment, or use the dashboard). These
#    are read INSIDE Convex functions and are NOT read from this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Convex Auth v2 signing keys. `convex/convex.config.ts` declares them
# in `defineApp({ env: … })`, so a deployment without them fails to push.
# On dev: `npx @convex-dev/auth@2.0.0-alpha.1` generates and sets both (add --force to rotate).
# On prod: see the "Deploy" section of the README — the setup CLI has no --prod
# flag, so point it at prod with CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT or set the keys by hand.
# Never paste key material into this file.
#   AUTH_PRIVATE_KEY   base64 of the PKCS8 RS256 private key PEM
#   AUTH_JWKS          JSON Web Key Set, served at /auth/.well-known/jwks.json

# Optional — base URL used to build the "manage your booking" links in emails.
# Despite the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix this is read server-side inside Convex
# functions (convex/public.ts, convex/admin.ts), so it belongs on the Convex
# deployment. No Next.js code reads it.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://convexbooking.dev

# Optional — booking confirmation / cancellation emails via Resend.
# Without RESEND_API_KEY no email is sent at all (the public sandbox sets none,
# which is the recommended setting for a shared demo).
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=bookings@example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Vercel project side — set in the Vercel dashboard / `vercel env add`.
#    Not read from this file either.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. Production deploy key from the Convex dashboard
# (Settings -> Deploy keys -> Generate production deploy key). The build command
# in vercel.json uses it to push the Convex backend and to inject
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL into `npm run build`.
#   CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY=prod:...

# Optional. Only useful on Vercel if you later add Next.js code that reads it;
# the emails read it from the Convex deployment (see section 2).
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://convexbooking.dev

# WorkOS is no longer used by this app. If a deployment still carries the old
# vars, remove them: `npx convex env remove --prod WORKOS_API_KEY` etc., and
# delete WORKOS_CLIENT_ID / WORKOS_API_KEY / WORKOS_COOKIE_PASSWORD /
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKOS_REDIRECT_URI from Vercel and from .env.local.
